# deaddrop-hunter - Suricata rules (informational)
# Public blockchain JSON-RPC endpoints contacted from the internal network.
# Legitimate wallets, dApps and developer tools use these hosts too: treat hits as
# hunting leads and correlate with the process (EDR/Sysmon) - see rules/sigma/README.md.
# SID range: 9100000-9100999 (local). Tested for syntax with suricata-check; requires Suricata >= 7.
# License: MIT. Author: deaddrop-hunter contributors. Date: 2026-10-19.

# --- DNS queries ---
alert dns $HOME_NET any -> any any (msg:"DEADDROP-HUNTER INFO DNS query for public blockchain RPC endpoint (Polygon RPC)"; dns.query; content:"polygon-rpc|2e|com"; nocase; endswith; pcre:"/(^|\.)polygon-rpc\.com$/i"; reference:url,www.linkedin.com/pulse/hunting-etherhiding-from-one-cluster-ecosystem-alex-necula-r7l8e/; classtype:policy-violation; priority:4; metadata:created_at 2026_10_19, updated_at 2026_10_19, signature_severity Informational, mitre_technique_id T1102_001; sid:9100001; rev:1;)
